When a new key is added, the implementation checks whether the storage is full. If it is, it throws StorageFullException.

Why throw an exception? The storage class should report that it cannot accept a new entry. The Cache class then decides which existing entry should be removed.
Class 3: EvictionPolicy<K>
interface EvictionPolicy<K> {
    void keyAccessed(K key);
    K evictKey();
}


This interface separates the eviction algorithm from the cache implementation.
- keyAccessed(key) informs the policy that a key has been accessed.
- evictKey() returns the key that should be removed.
The policy can be LRU, LFU, FIFO, or another algorithm. Each policy can implement the same interface.
