7. Time complexity
Operation	Average time complexity
Add a node at the end	\(O(1)\)
Detach a known node	\(O(1)\)
Find a node using the HashMap	\(O(1)\)
Mark a key as recently used	\(O(1)\) average
Evict the LRU key	\(O(1)\) average
Get a cached value	\(O(1)\) average

The linked list and map together use \(O(n)\) space for \(n\) tracked keys.
8. Design patterns and interview points
- Strategy pattern: EvictionPolicy allows different eviction algorithms to be plugged into the cache.
- Factory pattern: A CacheFactory can construct a cache with default storage and eviction policy.
- Dependency injection: Cache receives its dependencies through its constructor.
- Generic programming: <K, V> supports different key and value types.
- Separation of concerns: Storage, eviction logic, linked-list management, and cache coordination are handled by separate classes.
